ow. Once again, I apologize for this lack of responsibility, and thank you all for your help.\nBonus: When I encountered the error, I didn't know what \"semantic\" meant, but later, when I studied the principles of programming languages, I understood where the problem came from.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/3752938476/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/3754332642","html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/9099#issuecomment-3754332642","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/9099","id":3754332642,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJYd5Dc7fxpHi","user":{"login":"Sp3ctral","id":65112446,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MTEyNDQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65112446?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sp3ctral","html_url":"https://github.com/Sp3ctral","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sp3ctral/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sp3ctral/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sp3ctral/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sp3ctral/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sp3ctral/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sp3ctral/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sp3ctral/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sp3ctral/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sp3ctral/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-15T11:44:47Z","updated_at":"2026-01-15T11:44:47Z","body":"> Hello everyone! First of all, I apologize for bringing up the issue without explaining it clearly. This problem arose when I was learning programming. At that time, there were special characters in the code that Copilot didn't recognize. I deleted them, and the error disappeared. Perhaps this semantic error no longer occurs now. Once again, I apologize for this lack of responsibility, and thank you all for your help. Bonus: When I encountered the error, I didn't know what \"semantic\" meant, but later, when I studied the principles of programming languages, I understood where the problem came from.\n\nNo problem! Thanks for starting the issue. It's surprising to see it happening again considering it was marked as patched in previous issues. Happy learning!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/3754332642/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]}